le": "Monthly tax table: tax withheld from monthly pay - Wage Calculator", "description": "See the monthly tax table amounts withheld from pay \u2014 threshold, no-threshold and study-loan columns computed from the ATO Schedule 1 formula."}, {"url": "https://www.superguide.com.au/super-booster/income-tax-rates-brackets", "title": "Australian income tax brackets and rates (2026-27 and previous years)", "description": "# Australian income tax brackets and rates (2026-27 and previous years)\n## Income tax rates for 2026\u201327 (Australian residents)\n| **Income thresholds** | **Tax rate** | **Tax payable on this income** |\n|-|-|-|\n| $0 \u2013 $18,200 | 0% | Nil |\n| $18,201 \u2013 $45,000 | 15% | 15c for each $1 over $18,200 |\n| $45,001 \u2013 $135,000 | 30% | $4,020 plus 30c for each $1 over $45,000 |\n| $135,001 \u2013 $190,000 | 37% | $31,020 plus 37c for each $1 over $135,000 |\n| $190,001 and over | 45% | $51,370 plus 45c for each $1 over $190,000 |\n\n## Income tax rates for 2025\u201326 (Australian residents)\n### How tax paid has changed since 2023\u201324\n| Income | 2023\u201324 tax paid | 2024\u201325 tax paid | 2026\u201327 tax paid | Total tax cut since 2023\u201324 |\n|-|-|-|-|-|\n| $20,000 | $342 | $288 | $270 | $72 |\n| $30,000 | $2,242 | $1,888 | $1,770 | $472 |\n| $40,000 | $4,142 | $3,488 | $3,270 | $872 |\n| $50,000 | $6,717 | $5,788 | $5,520 | $1,197 |\n| $60,000 | $9,967 | $8,788 | $8,520 | $1,447 |\n| $70,000 | $13,217 | $11,788 | $11,520 | $1,697 |\n| $80,000 | $16,467 | $14,788 | $14,520 | $1,947 |\n| $90,000 | $19,717 | $17,788 | $17,520 | $2,197 |\n| $100,000 | $22,967 | $20,788 | $20,520 | $2,447 |\n| $110,000 | $26,217 | $23,788 | $23,520 | $2,697 |\n| $120,000 | $29,467 | $26,788 | $26,520 | $2,947 |\n| $130,000 | $33,167 | $29,788 | $29,520 | $3,647 |\n| $140,000 | $36,867 | $33,138 | $32,870 | $3,997 |\n| $150,000 | $40,567 | $36,838 | $36,570 | $3,997 |\n| $160,000 | $44,267 | $40,538 | $40,270 | $3,997 |\n| $170,000 | $47,967 | $44,238 | $43,970 | $3,997 |\n| $180,000 | $51,667 | $47,938 | $47,670 | $3,997 |\n| $190,000 | $56,167 | $51,638 | $51,370 | $4,797 |\n| $200,000 | $60,667 | $56,138 | $55,870 | $4,797 |\n\n## Income tax offsets, levies and surcharges\n### Private health insurance rebate+\n#### Rebate rates from 1 July 2026 to 31 March 2027\n| **Age of oldest person covered** | **Base tier** | **Tier 1** | **Tier 2** | **Tier 3** |\n|-|-|-|-|-|\n| Under 65 | 24.118% | 16.079% | 8.038% | 0% |\n| 65 to 69 | 28.139% | 20.098% | 12.058% | 0% |\n| 70 and over | 32.158% | 24.118% | 16.079% | 0% |"}, {"url": "https://www.gibsonclark.com.au/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2013/06/Monthly-Tax-Tables.pdf", "title": "[PDF] Monthly withholding table | Gibson Clark", "description": "You should read this publication together with Weekly tax table \u2013 including instructions for calculating monthly and quarterly withholding (NAT 1005). Page 2. 2."}, {"url": "https://onestoptax.com.au/tax-tables/", "title": "Tax Tables - One Stop Tax", "description": "ATO produces a range of tax tables to help employers work out how much to withhold from payments they make to their employees or other payees."}, {"url": "https://taxbyte.com.au/monthly-tax-table/", "title": "Monthly Tax Table: ATO PAYG Withholding Guide 2026", "description": "7 July 2026 \u00b7 The monthly tax table is the ATO's official reference for calculating Pay As You Go (PAYG) withholding when wages, salary, or allowances are ..."}]}